"""PLANTED FAULT for probe_audit.py's NEVER MATCHED detector. This file must be flagged.

Aimed at the invariant: a regex site in a checker that matches nothing across a whole real run
must be reported. It cannot expire, because it does not name any pattern that is wrong today.

The plant travels the same route as a real checker -- probe_audit runs it as a subprocess through
trace_child with the instrumented re module, exactly as it runs verify.py. A fault handed to the
detector by any other route would prove a detector nothing uses.

The bug below is the one this project actually hit: the pattern was written against a shape the
source does not use, so it parsed the two sites that already agreed and never saw the third.
"""
import re
import sys

root = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else "."
problems = []

SOURCE = """
local Colours = {}
Colours.Primary   = Color3.fromRGB(208, 149, 241)
Colours.Secondary = Color3.fromRGB(24, 24, 24)
Colours.Accent    = Color3.new(0.82, 0.58, 0.95)
"""

# Alive: this one parses two of the three sites and can fail.
rgb = re.findall(r"Color3\.fromRGB\((\d+), (\d+), (\d+)\)", SOURCE)
if len(rgb) < 2:
    problems.append("colours: fewer than two RGB colours found")

# THE PLANT. Color3.new takes floats, and this pattern demands integers, so the one site carrying
# a colour the audit cannot read is the one it never looks at. Zero matches, every run, forever.
floats = re.findall(r"Color3\.new\((\d+), (\d+), (\d+)\)", SOURCE)  # MUST FLAG
for r, g, b in floats:
    if int(r) > 255:
        problems.append("colours: a component above 255")

print("\n".join(problems) if problems else "fixture: no problems")
sys.exit(0)
